 Local Printer Setup

1. Connect the printer to the computer using a USB cable, or connect the printer and computer to the same Wi-Fi/network.

2. Turn on the printer and make sure it is ready.

3. Open **Settings > Bluetooth & devices > Printers & scanners** in Windows.

4. Click **Add device** and select the printer when it appears.

5. If Windows does not install the printer automatically, download and install the **correct driver** for the printer model from the manufacturer's website.

6. After installation, open **Printers & scanners**, select the printer, and choose **Printer properties**.

7. Click **Print Test Page**.

8. Check that the printer produces the test page correctly. If it prints successfully, the printer installation is complete.
